From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:21:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] x86/boot: Mark a kernel that relocated itself as randomized

__relocate_kernel() moves the kernel's virtual base and does not tell
the rest of the kernel. kaslr_enabled() reads KASLR_FLAG in the boot
parameters, which only the decompressor sets, so a kernel entered
through PVH that randomized itself still kept the direct map, vmalloc
and vmemmap at their fixed bases (RANDOMIZE_MEMORY did nothing), and
reported no kernel offset.

Set KASLR_FLAG once the relocations have been applied, and apply none
from a table the relocs tool never filled, which would otherwise mark a
kernel that did not move as randomized.

Carried by spin-stack/machine for #645 on top of Hou Wenlong's RFC
(lore cover.1769434279.git.houwenlong.hwl@antgroup.com, 2026-01-26),
which does neither.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/x86/boot/startup/kaslr.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/boot/startup/kaslr.c b/arch/x86/boot/startup/kaslr.c
index 975e883af..8594ca34e 100644
--- a/arch/x86/boot/startup/kaslr.c
+++ b/arch/x86/boot/startup/kaslr.c
@@ -104,6 +104,10 @@ void __init __relocate_kernel(unsigned long p2v_offset, struct boot_params *bp)
 	if (cmdline_find_option_bool((char *)cmd_line_ptr, "nokaslr"))
 		return;
 
+	/* An empty table: the relocs tool never filled it, so nothing can move. */
+	if (!reloc[-1])
+		return;
+
 	boot_params_ptr = bp;
 	virt_addr = find_random_virt_addr(LOAD_PHYSICAL_ADDR, image_size);
 	delta = virt_addr - LOAD_PHYSICAL_ADDR;
@@ -117,4 +121,11 @@ void __init __relocate_kernel(unsigned long p2v_offset, struct boot_params *bp)
 		ptr = (unsigned long)(*reloc + p2v_offset);
 		*(uint64_t *)ptr += delta;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * What the decompressor sets when it randomized the kernel, and what
+	 * kaslr_enabled() reads: without it RANDOMIZE_MEMORY leaves the direct
+	 * map, vmalloc and vmemmap at their fixed bases.
+	 */
+	bp->hdr.loadflags |= KASLR_FLAG;
 }
-- 
